1.. Presentation of a Certificate of Recognition for the 25th Annual Matt and Mike Johnson Memorial Blood Drive.
PRESENT {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Mayor Lesser announced that the Annual Memorial Blood Drive, traditionally held during the Manhattan Beach Hometown Fair, will take place this year at the Manhattan Beach Library on Saturday, October 4, 2025, and Sunday, October 5, 2025 from 10:00 AM to 4:00 PM; announced that there is an enormous need for blood donations, whether for infusions, planned surgeries, or cancer treatments; and noted that in recent years, there has been a shortage, therefore, this blood drive, among others, is incredibly important to support the community\rquote s healthcare needs.\line\line Memorial Blood Drive Chairman Michael Archuleta shared that over the 25 years of the blood drive, 1,363 units of usable blood have been donated through 1,440 donors; and announced that they also wished to honor Matt\rquote s father, who passed away last year due to cancer; and therefore, the memorial blood drive is now officially named the Matt and Mike Johnson Memorial Blood Drive.\line\line\pard On behalf of the City Council, Mayor Lesser presented a Certificate of Recognition for the 25\super th\nosupersub  Annual Matt and Mike Johnson Memorial Blood Drive.\cf1\i0\f1\par
}


